1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,753
Scott Hanley pours at Candlelight Tavern.

2
00:00:02,753 --> 00:00:03,810
South Pearl.

3
00:00:03,810 --> 00:00:04,879
Wash Park.

4
00:00:04,879 --> 00:00:08,209
He's been behind that stick going on twenty-seven years.

5
00:00:08,209 --> 00:00:11,262
Chris Johnson's been with him most of that stretch.

6
00:00:11,262 --> 00:00:18,581
They've known each other since the early nineties — Himalaya in Aurora, then other bars, then Candlelight under Dave and Lisa Bryan.

7
00:00:18,581 --> 00:00:22,776
In twenty seventeen, Lisa told Westword Scott's a legend.

8
00:00:22,776 --> 00:00:23,907
She meant it.

9
00:00:23,907 --> 00:00:26,034
In twenty eighteen he got sick.

10
00:00:26,034 --> 00:00:29,711
The neighborhood showed up — fundraisers, a pub crawl, a GoFundMe.

11
00:00:29,711 --> 00:00:31,310
He came back to the bar.

12
00:00:31,310 --> 00:00:38,413
November tenth, twenty twenty-five — Colorado Restaurant Association named him HOSPY Bartender of the Year.

13
00:00:38,413 --> 00:00:40,144
Wash Park already knew.

14
00:00:40,144 --> 00:00:41,382
Pull up a stool.

15
00:00:41,382 --> 00:00:42,536
He's still there.

